1.1.text:
Article 9
Curative efforts as referred to in Article 6 are as follows: a. optimizing technical services related to complaints of violence against women and children;
b. providing adequate facilities and infrastructure for handling health rehabilitation, social rehabilitation, repatriation, social reintegration, and legal assistance;
c. conducting handling for victims of crime and violence in a fast, precise, and accurate manner by law enforcement officials.

Article 5
In order to realize the objectives as referred to in Article 3 letter b, efforts shall be made through:
a. establishment, development, and capacity strengthening of institutions for the protection of women and children including service units for complaints of violence against women and children, as well as legal aid services;
b. improvement of the quality of human resources of managers;
c. strengthening of institutional capacity for Gender Mainstreaming (PUG) and children;
d. strengthening and development of gender and child data systems.

Article 7
Promotive efforts as referred to in Article 6 are as follows: a. strengthening coordination mechanisms and networks between service units in efforts to handle cases of violence;
b. providing Communication, Information, and Education (IEC) materials related to prevention and handling of violence;
c. conducting socialization, advocacy and social campaigns in the context of prevention and handling of violence.

Article 8
Preventive measures as referred to in Article 6 are as follows:
a. conducting legal awareness education for the community, especially for women and children;
b. conducting massive and sustainable movements involving the community in prevention and handling of violence;
c. instilling character values, morals, and family resilience;
d. involving the role and participation of the community in women's empowerment and child protection.

REGENT OF SAMPANG
EAST JAVA PROVINCE
REGIONAL REGULATION OF SAMPANG REGENCY NUMBER 7 YEAR 2017
CONCERNING
WOMEN'S EMPOWERMENT AND CHILD PROTECTION
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF SAMPANG,

Considering : a. that every citizen has equal rights to live a dignified life in accordance with the principles of humanity, equality, and justice;
b. that women's empowerment is carried out so that women can actualize their potential optimally to participate in development according to their capacity;
c. that women who are vulnerable groups need to receive special protection so that they do not experience violence and can live a decent life according to the principles of humanity, equality and justice;
d. that with the enactment of Regulation of the Minister of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 6 Year 2015 Concerning the System of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection, the regional government needs to improve the quality of life of women and protect children.
e. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, letter c, and letter d, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;

- 2 - In View of :1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law number 12 Year 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Regions within East Java Province as amended by Law Number 2 Year 1965 concerning Amendment of the Territorial Boundaries of Surabaya Municipality and Surabaya Level II Region (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1965 Number 19, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 2730);
3. Law Number 23 Year 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as amended by Law Number 35 Year 2014 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 297, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5606);
4. Law Number 21 Year 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
5. Law Number 12 Year 2011 concerning the Formation of Laws and Regulations (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2011 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234);
